Cell["\<\
then starting from \[ImaginaryI], it produces any point x[1] + \[ImaginaryI] \
y. That is, the upper-half plane real and imaginary parts are determined by \
the group coordinates themselves directly, instead of being some function of \
those coordinates. 

But here, keep x[3] for now.
An SL(2)/SO(2) group element is then:\
\>", "Text",
